Z||000000||Elenor84||12-11-2001||02:27 AM||||Just curious if its possible or even worth saving the money by doing this myself?<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||watts||12-11-2001||02:33 AM||||I'd give that a no.<P>I'm assuming you're pulling the engine right out, right?  If so, get it boiled - it's the only way to get all the inner passages, etc clean.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||12-11-2001||02:47 AM||||Yep she's stripped right down...thx for the advice!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Banzai||12-11-2001||06:42 AM||||The machine shop will hot dip it before and after they do any machining. BUT you will still have to clean it with soap and water (hot water if you can) before you assemble it. After you clean it wipe the cylinders with auto tranny fluid.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!1||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||12-11-2001||11:19 AM||||Yup don't trust the hot dip.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Butter||12-11-2001||12:55 PM||||I would inquire about the normal boiling proceedure of any given place before I had anyone dip a block for me anymore.  Just boiling the block is not a good method for cleaning one.  I have found that if the folks doing the block boiling do not clean their vat regular or allow nasty blocks with excessive build up on them to be boiled regularly, then I have a hard time getting the oil journals clean.  This is especially true if the vat has an agitator.  Oil journals should be cleaned with a bore brush and flushed if the passages have been contaminated.  After some bad experiences I found a place that will boil and clean the oil journals by removing oil journal caps and doing it right.<P>If the oil has not been contaminated and no machining has been done to the block I have had good luck just cleaning the block with a strong soap and flushing the oil journals.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/buttersig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||REDHOTT88||12-11-2001||02:05 PM||||<BR>Butter... Is it me or does the Fiero in your SIG look DUSTY?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed <BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Red and shiny all over!)</FONT>||||reg||1
