Z||000008||Butter||12-11-2001||03:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by REDHOTT88:<BR><B><BR>Butter... Is it me or does the Fiero in your SIG look DUSTY?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>It's Jack Frost.<BR>He likes Fiero's too.<P>The horse in the background right over the sun roof, the frost covering the bad paint, the Southern setting, and the shop in the background behind the far left pine, are what make me partial to the pic.<P><BR>I elected to put a v8 in it rather than do a paint job at this point.  <P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/buttersig_1.gif"> ||||reg||7
Z||000009||GTDude||12-12-2001||11:59 AM||||Find a reputable machine shop...one that also rebuilds engines is best...and have them hot dip it.  The machine shop I deal with is very methodical about cleaning all the passages and washing it down with soap and water.  Just have to find the right one.  Ask questions.<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
